# Kontakt 8.13 at 100 % (shoot.sh, DPI=96, NODRIVE=1), oracle run 2026-11-25 (gen.py textpos()).
# Top row of the words' ink below the control's top, in px, for TEXTPOS_Y unset, 0, -4, 3, 6, 10
# and 500 (columns). Rows are stock controls 16, 20 and 30 px tall and two 90 x 20 pictured menus.
control              unset  0   -4  3   6   10  500
menu 16/20/30        9      9   9   12  15  19  hidden
value edit 16/20/30  10     10  10  12  13  15  hidden
button 16/20/30      9      9   9   12  15  19  hidden
pictured menu        9      9   9   12  15  19  hidden
pictured menu, 13 R  7      7   7   10  13  17  hidden
# Unset and negative values count as 0, and the height never moves the words: they sit in the same
# 20-px cell at 16, 20 and 30 px, clipped by the control. A menu's or a button's words drop by
# TEXTPOS_Y; a value edit's by half of it, rounded up. 500 puts them out of sight.
# A pictured menu draws its words in the stock pixel font at the stock menu's 7-px inset; in font 13
# right-aligned they run under the picture's right edge and are clipped there. KONTRA matches the
# stock rows and the default-font pictured row. In font 13, right-aligned, its words sit 1 px lower
# and about 4 px further left (open: this page cannot measure the clipped inset).
# Not matched: a 30-px value edit at TEXTPOS_Y 10 clips its words a row higher than KONTRA does.
